                    <p class="notebook-p coming-soon-regular fw-bold underline" style="font-size:1rem;">Modular Binomials</p>
                    <p class="notebook-p coming-soon-regular">
                        Rearrange the following equations to get the primes p,q<br><br>
                        N = p × q<br>
                        c<sub>1</sub> = (2 × p + 3 × q)<sup>e₁</sup> mod N<br>
                        c<sub>2</sub> = (5 × p + 7 × q)<sup>e₂</sup> mod N

                    </p>
                    <p class="notebook-p coming-soon-regular dotted " style="background-color: rgba(151, 240, 42, 0.13);">
                    <strong class="underline highlight-green">Combinari de n luate cate k</strong><br>
                    <strong>C(n, k) = n! / (k! * (n - k)!)</strong><br>
                    <strong class="underline highlight-green">Binomul lui Newton</strong><br>
                        (a + b)<sup>n</sup> = 
  &sum;<sub>k=0</sub><sup>n</sup> (C
  <sup>n</sup><sub>k</sub>) &middot; a<sup>n - k</sup> &middot; b<sup>k</sup><br>
                    </p>
                    <p class=" notebook-p coming-soon-regular">
                        <br>
                        Solutie:
                    </p>
                    <code class="notebook-p coming-soon-regular dotted">
N =... e1 =... e2 =... c1 =... c2 =...

a1 = 2 b1 = 3 a2 = 5 b2 = 7

a1_inv = inverse_mod(a1, N)
b1_inv = inverse_mod(b1, N)
a2_inv = inverse_mod(a2, N)
b2_inv = inverse_mod(b2, N)

m = power_mod(a2 * a1_inv, e1 * e2, N)
m2 = power_mod(b2 * b1_inv, e1 * e2, N)


c1_exp = power_mod(c1, e2, N)
c2_exp = power_mod(c2, e1, N)


q_pow = (m * c1_exp - c2_exp) % N
p_pow = (m2 * c1_exp - c2_exp) % N

# Compute gcd with N
# the division is not needed beause N=p*q
# gcd(q,N) = q
# gcd(q * u, N) = q (because u doesn's divide N)
q = gcd(q_pow, N)
p = gcd(p_pow, N)

print("Recovered primes:")
print("p =", p)
print("q =", q)

